226,"prompt_7":465,"prompt_8":371,"prompt_9":268,"prompt_17":136},"was_row_colours":{"1":"teal","2":"blue","3":"blue","4":"red","5":"red","6":"green","7":"green","8":"pink","9":"pink"}},"widgets_values":["t2va","16:9",1,0,0,"visual_style:\nHigh-quality 2D hand-drawn animated short: clean inked outlines, flat cel-painted colours, expressive poses, painterly storm skies and rolling sea, and classic television animation timing.\n\nvisual_consistency:\nKeep the keeper, her dog, the lighthouse, the fishing boat, line weight and the stormy blue-grey palette consistent throughout.","overall_soundscape:\nClean animated-short production audio with wind, rain and sea ambience and synchronized foley.","id=\"x001\"\nduration_seconds: 4.5\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Wide exterior establishing shot at dusk. A white-and-red lighthouse stands alone on a rocky island while storm clouds roll in from the sea. Waves break against the rocks and rain begins to slant across the frame. The lighthouse lamp is still dark.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA low, brooding orchestral swell with soft timpani and strings.",4.5,0,"cut",-1,"both","id=\"x002\"\nduration_seconds: 8\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Interior of the lamp room at the top of the lighthouse. Mara, a sturdy woman in her forties with a grey braid and a yellow raincoat, stands beside the great glass lens. Pip, a small scruffy white terrier with one brown ear, sits at her feet. Rain streaks the windows behind them.\n\nMara pats the lens housing. Mara's calm, warm female voice (S1) says: <d>[English] Storm's early tonight, Pip. Let's get this light turning.</d>\n\nPip wags his tail and gives one sharp bark.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA gentle, steady strings motif under the rain.",8,0,"cut",-1,"both","id=\"x003\"\nduration_seconds: 7\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Mara grips the brass crank beside the lens and turns it with both hands. The clockwork mechanism clicks into motion, the lamp flares to life, and the lens begins to rotate, throwing a broad beam out through the rain. Pip circles her feet, watching the light.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nThe strings lift as the lamp comes on.",7,16,"carry",-1,"both","id=\"x004\"\nduration_seconds: 6\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Exterior at sea in the storm. A small green fishing boat pitches over dark waves. An old fisherman in an orange oilskin and a knit cap clings to the wheel, squinting into the rain.\n\nThe fisherman's gruff, weathered male voice (S1) says: <d>[English] Come on, come on. Where's that light?</d>\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nTense low brass and rolling drums.",6,34,"carry (audio only)",-1,"both","id=\"x005\"\nduration_seconds: 8\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Back in the lamp room. The beam sweeps past the rain-streaked windows. Mara, in her yellow raincoat with her grey braid, raises a pair of brass binoculars and spots a tiny green boat far out on the waves. Pip, the small white terrier with one brown ear, stands on his hind legs at the window.\n\nMara lowers the binoculars. Mara's calm, warm female voice (S1) says: <d>[English] There he is. Pip, the bell!</d>\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nThe strings quicken with urgency.",8,34,"carry (audio only)",-1,"both","id=\"x006\"\nduration_seconds: 7\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] Pip races to a rope hanging by the stairs, grabs it in his teeth and tugs with all his weight. A brass bell above the doorway rings out loud and clear while Mara steadies the turning lens, keeping the beam on the distant boat.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA warm, rising resolution with strings and soft horns as the bell rings.",7,16,"carry",-1,"both","",7,0,"cut",-1,"both","",5.5,0,"cut",-1,"both","",7,0,"cut",-1,"both","",8,16,"carry",-1,"both","",10,16,"carry",-1,"both","",5.5,0,"cut",-1,"both","",8,16,"carry",-1,"both","",8,16,"carry",-1,"both","",7,16,"carry",-1,"both","",8,0,"cut",-1,"both","",10,16,"carry",-1,"both","